---
title: "My GitHub looked healthy. The business didn't."
description: "Green squares made me feel productive while I avoided the hard parts."
date: "2026-07-22"
tags:
  - building
  - founding
published: true
layout: docs
---

Some nights I'd ship until 2am and screenshot the contribution graph like it meant something. The code was real. The company still needed follow-ups I didn't want to send.

Building Algility made that obvious. A clean PR doesn't collect. A reply from a buyer does.

I still write a lot of code. I just don't use commits as proof the business is fine. If I haven't talked to a customer that week, I'm kidding myself.
